# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 ("Binding groups and cycles": the order of a group's lines decides positions and nothing else; a building `match`'s arm adds no path segment), ch. 8 (`<-` binds the arm's plain result) and ruling TC (places counted as built): small gives 1 + 9, so the upper `match` takes `nil` and builds 0 and 1, the inner arm's label is 2, the arm's own label 3 and the last label 4; big gives 2 + 9, the inner arm builds nothing; soft gives 20, so the upper `match` builds 0 and the last label is 1.
test small

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Label(text="under")
    1: Ui.Label(text="at 10")
    2: Ui.Label(text="small")
    3: Ui.Label(text="loud 1")
    4: Ui.Label(text="below 10")

